# ScalarLM recipe: symlink to the client venv (box-local, RAM-backed)
.env_scalarlm

# --- MI355X build workspace (local only, never committed) ---------------------
# NOTE the leading slashes: these are ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored
# `models/` matches every directory named models at any depth — including
# training/llm/scalarlm/ml/cray_megatron/models/, which would silently drop
# load_model.py (the FA2 downgrade and the embedding materializer) from the
# commit and ship a broken tree.
#
# ScalarLM_greg is a full nested git clone of supermassive-intelligence/scalarlm
# carrying the AMD integration. `git add -A` would otherwise stage it as a
# gitlink — a submodule pointer to commits that exist on no remote, which clones
# as an empty directory. It is a build input, not repo content.
/ScalarLM_greg/
# HF model cache created by the server runs; re-downloadable.
/models/
# Benchmark fixture generated for the DDP/FSDP comparison.
/bench_data.jsonl

# --- vendored ScalarLM server source -----------------------------------------
# training/llm/scalarlm/repo/ is a VERBATIM upstream tree. This project's own
# ignore rules are written for this project's files and must not reach into it:
# unanchored patterns above (`plot.py`, `lib/`) otherwise silently drop real
# upstream source — 9 files, including sdk/masint/cli/plot.py, ui/src/lib/*, and
# cmd/lib/colors.sh — producing a vendored tree that looks complete and is not.
!training/llm/scalarlm/repo/**

# ...but never vendor build/run artifacts back in.
training/llm/scalarlm/repo/**/__pycache__/
training/llm/scalarlm/repo/**/*.pyc
training/llm/scalarlm/repo/models/
training/llm/scalarlm/repo/.venv/
training/llm/scalarlm/repo/**/node_modules/

# repo/ml/ is NOT source. There is exactly one ml/ tree in this repository —
# training/llm/scalarlm/ml/ — and build_image.sh copies it into repo/ at build
# time so the image always bakes the current recipe. Committing a second copy
# here is what makes the two drift.
training/llm/scalarlm/repo/ml/
FSDP2_CHANGES_FOR_H100.md
h100_needed_updates.md
